  "changed": [
    "Pro 2: Replaced 'Effective team management features like roles, permissions, and folder structures.' with 'Efficient item creation and organization for various data types.' based on '[benefit] The Add button offers Login, Card, Identity, Note, SSH key and Folder in one dropdown, so starting a CRM login or a server-access note took two clicks.' and '[benefit] A login or secure note saves with only the Item name filled (username and password optional), so the CRM entry and the server-access note were each created in about three actions.' and '[benefit] The vault and the org collections view both have a filter panel by type (Login, Card, Identity, Secure note, SSH key), plus Collections, Trash and a search box.'",
    "Con 3: Replaced 'Some advanced features might have a slight learning curve initially.' with 'Initial setup for team sharing and advanced features can be less intuitive.' based on '[friction] The personal vault Add menu has no Collection option; sharing requires first creating an organization from a 'New organization' link tucked into the vault filter sidebar.' and '[friction] Custom fields are not visible in the initial Add login dialog view; they sit further down the scrolled form, so I did not reach them in the time I had.' and '[friction] After creating the organization the app jumps from Password Manager into a separate Admin Console with its own sidebar, so my saved CRM and note items were not visible where collections and members are managed.'"
